WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.270
Cymbal just bought a fashion brand.

2
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.155
And it runs on AWS.

3
00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:06.890
Leadership wants one view of all the data.

4
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.325
But customer data from Europe has to stay in Europe.

5
00:00:10.345 --> 00:00:11.900
Two ideas solve this.

6
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.675
Keep things portable, and make data easy to find.

7
00:00:15.695 --> 00:00:18.435
Idea one: do not lock yourself in.

8
00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:20.210
Think of a power plug adapter.

9
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.945
The same device works in any country.

10
00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:25.370
Apache Beam is like that for pipelines.

11
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.105
The same code runs on Dataflow, Flink or Spark.

12
00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:33.740
Dataproc runs your open source Spark and Hadoop jobs with no changes.

13
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.515
And open formats, like Iceberg and Parquet, keep your data readable by any engine.

14
00:00:39.535 --> 00:00:40.615
Now the hard part.

15
00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:43.050
The data in AWS must not move.

16
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.387
So do not move the data.

17
00:00:44.407 --> 00:00:45.910
Move the query.

18
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.973
BigQuery Omni runs your query inside AWS or Azure.

19
00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:52.070
Only the results come back.

20
00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.195
BigLake adds table security on top of plain files:

21
00:00:55.215 --> 00:00:58.030
rows and columns, like a warehouse.

22
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:04.180
The trap is copying S3 data into Google Cloud when it must stay in AWS.

23
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.265
Idea two: data nobody can find might as well not exist.

24
00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:11.227
Dataplex organizes data without moving it.

25
00:01:11.247 --> 00:01:13.600
Think of it as a map of your data.

26
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.838
A lake is a domain, like Sales.

27
00:01:15.858 --> 00:01:17.875
A zone is raw or curated.

28
00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:20.585
An asset is a bucket or a dataset.

29
00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:22.635
The catalog is the search box.

30
00:01:22.655 --> 00:01:26.320
It collects metadata on its own, so people can search.

31
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.483
And lineage shows what feeds what.

32
00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:30.730
Check it before you change a column.

33
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.617
The trap: building your own metadata database.

34
00:01:33.637 --> 00:01:36.880
A managed catalog already exists.

35
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.140
Recap.

36
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.502
Keep compute portable with Beam and Spark.

37
00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:41.815
Keep data open.

38
00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.850
And when data cannot move, query it in place.

39
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:49.460
Then organize with Dataplex, search with the catalog, and track lineage.

40
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.097
Your turn.

41
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.855
Try the checkpoint below.
